.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH git-veil-changes 1  "git-veil-changes " 
.SH NAME
git\-veil\-changes \- Report where plaintext differs from the last hidden version
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit\-veil changes\fR [\fB\-\-email\fR] [\fB\-\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-key\-store\fR] [\fB\-\-passphrase\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIFILES\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Report where plaintext differs from the last hidden version
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-email\fR \fI<EMAIL>\fR
Your email address
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\fR \fI<REMOTE>\fR [default: origin]
Git remote name
.TP
\fB\-\-key\-store\fR \fI<KEY_STORE>\fR
Key store directory (default: $HOME/.git\-veil)
.TP
\fB\-\-passphrase\-stdin\fR
Read the passphrase for a passphrase\-protected private key from stdin (exactly one line). Wins over the GITVEIL_PASSPHRASE environment variable; never pass a passphrase as a CLI argument
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIFILES\fR]
File(s) to check (default: all tracked files)
.SH EXTRA
Reports where the on\-disk plaintext differs from the last hidden version:
each tracked file\*(Aqs .secret ciphertext is decrypted and compared with the
plaintext beside it. Differences are data, not errors. Files with no
ciphertext, or no plaintext on disk, are skipped with a note and are not
counted as changed.

EXAMPLES
  $ git\-veil changes                # check every tracked file
  $ git\-veil changes .env           # check one file
  $ git\-veil changes \-\-passphrase\-stdin < pass.txt
